// Safe Mode reboot attempt
//
// Fires when ASR catches something trying to reboot the machine into Safe Mode. Security
// tools don't run in Safe Mode, and ransomware crews use it to get around them. ASR
// doesn't raise an alert for this on its own.
//
// Runs:      Continuous (NRT)
// Severity:  High
// MITRE:     T1688
// Tables:    DeviceEvents
// Custom details: ActionType
//
// Needs:
//   - The ASR rule "Block rebooting machine in Safe Mode" in Audit or Block. If it isn't,
//     "Safe Mode boot set with bcdedit" still covers you.
//
// Triage (paste into Recommended actions):
//   - Check the command line and the account.
//   - Escalate unless IT is fixing the device under a ticket.
//   - Close if it's ticketed repair work.
//
// Based on: Microsoft's ASR rules reference, https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/defender-endpoint/attack-surface-reduction-rules-reference

DeviceEvents
| where ingestion_time() > ago(1d)
| where ActionType in ("AsrSafeModeRebootBlocked", "AsrSafeModeRebootedAudited", "AsrSafeModeRebootWarnBypassed")
| project Timestamp, ReportId, DeviceId, DeviceName, ActionType, FileName, ProcessCommandLine, InitiatingProcessFileName, InitiatingProcessCommandLine, InitiatingProcessAccountName
